  "source_text": "Title: Rotisserie-Style Chicken Gyros with Homemade Tzatziki\nServings: 4\n\nIngredients (component | amount unit | name | prep_style | pantry food_id):\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 30 ml | extra virgin olive oil |  | 000379\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 1 tsp | dried oregano |  | 000257\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 0.5 tsp | dried thyme |  | 000258\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 0.5 tsp | dried basil |  | 000256\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 1 tsp | Garlic Powder |  | 000643\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 1 tsp | Ground Onion |  | 000644\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 1 tsp | kosher salt |  | 000293\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 0.5 tsp | ground black pepper |  | 000285\n- Tzatziki Sauce | 250 g | greek yogurt |  | 000206\n- Tzatziki Sauce | 1 tsp | dill |  | 000249\n- Warm Pita Bread | 4 g | pita |  | 000340\n- Warm Pita Bread | 15 ml | olive oil |  | 000378\n- Vegetable Garnishes | 2 units | Roma tomatoes, chopped |  | IMP-6d4cd7\n- Vegetable Garnishes | 1 unit | red onion, medium, diced |  | IMP-fa00e5\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 600 g | chicken breast |  | 000044\n- Rotisserie-Style Chicken | 1 units | lemon |  | 000130\n- Tzatziki Sauce | 1 unit | Cucumber |  | 000642\n- Tzatziki Sauce | 2 unit | garlic |  | 000112\n- Tzatziki Sauce | 1 units | lemon |  | 000130\n\nSteps in order (component | phase | minutes | text):\n1. Rotisserie-Style Chicken | Prep |  | Flag: Raw Meat Handling. Wash hands and surfaces after contact. Slice the chicken breasts into very thin 1cm wide strips.\n2. Tzatziki Sauce | Prep |  | Grate the cucumber using a box grater. Wrap the pulp in a clean kitchen towel and squeeze out all excess moisture.\n3. Warm Pita Bread | Prep |  | Lightly brush both sides of each pita bread with olive oil.\n4. Vegetable Garnishes | Prep |  | Wash the Roma tomatoes and chop them into uniform cubes.\n5. Rotisserie-Style Chicken | Prep |  | In a large bowl, whisk together the olive oil, lemon juice, oregano, thyme, basil, onion powder, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n6. Tzatziki Sauce | Prep |  | Mince the garlic cloves and finely chop the fresh dill.\n7. Warm Pita Bread | Cook |  | Heat a large skillet over medium-high heat.\n8. Vegetable Garnishes | Prep |  | Peel the red onion and slice it into thin half-moons for a milder bite.\n9. Rotisserie-Style Chicken | Prep |  | Toss the chicken strips in the marinade until fully coated, cover, and refrigerate for 30 minutes.\n10. Tzatziki Sauce | Cook |  | In a small bowl, blend the Greek yogurt with the squeezed cucumber, garlic, lemon juice, and dill.\n11. Warm Pita Bread | Cook |  | Toast each pita for 1 minute per side until they are soft, warm, and have light golden spots.\n12. Vegetable Garnishes | Serve |  | Arrange the tomatoes and onions on a platter to be added to the gyros during final assembly.\n13. Rotisserie-Style Chicken | Cook |  | Preheat the oven to 200°C. Place a wire roasting rack over a foil-lined baking sheet.\n14. Tzatziki Sauce | Serve |  | Season with a pinch of salt to taste and chill in the refrigerator until ready for use.\n15. Warm Pita Bread | Serve |  | Stack the pitas and wrap them in a clean towel to keep them soft and steam slightly before serving.\n16. Rotisserie-Style Chicken | Cook |  | Arrange the marinated chicken strips in a single layer on the rack to allow air circulation, simulating a rotisserie environment.\n17. Rotisserie-Style Chicken | Cook |  | Roast for 20-25 minutes, or until the chicken reaches 74°C internal temperature and the edges are slightly charred.\n18. Rotisserie-Style Chicken | Serve |  | Remove from the oven and let the meat rest for 5 minutes before assembling the gyros.",
